                "start": 154,
                "username": "Nature"
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "We’re sharing the next major milestone in our non-invasive brain-to-text decoder research: Brain2Qwerty v2.\n\nBuilding on v1, which was published today in @Nature, Brain2Qwerty v2 is the highest-performing end-to-end pipeline capable of real-time sentence decoding from raw brain signals. It advances beyond character-level performance to decoding words and semantics, enabling accuracy for overall communication.\n\nWe believe this research has the potential to make a real difference for the millions of people who suffer from brain lesions or disorders that prevent them from communicating.\n\n🧵👇"
        },
